25.
Statutes. -
Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Statutes may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely :
(a)
the conferment of honorary degrees;
(b)
the formation of departments of teaching;
(c)
the fees to be charged for courses of study in the Institute and for admission to the examinations of degrees and
diplomas of the Institute;
(d)
the institution of fellowships, scholarships, exhibitions, medals and prizes;
(e)
the term of office and the method of appointment of officers of the Institute;
(f)
the qualifications of teachers of the Institute;
